<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Salona</h1><p class="st-meta">1205 CE – 1410 CE · capital Salona</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Frankish lordship around Amfissa and Delphi in central Greece that passed from French to Catalan to Byzantine hands before falling to the Ottomans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface of Montferrat</a> granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amfissa">Salona</a>, the medieval name of Amfissa, to the French knight Thomas d'Autremencourt in 1205. Its castle, built on the ancient acropolis, controlled the land between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-parnassus">Mount Parnassus</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-corinth">Gulf of Corinth</a>, including the old sanctuary of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delphi">Delphi</a> and the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galaxidi">Galaxidi</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amfissa">Salona</a> were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a> and neighbours of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-athens">Duchy of Athens</a>, ruling a Greek peasant population through a small Frankish elite. Thomas III d'Autremencourt was killed in 1311 fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-company">Catalan Company</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-halmyros">Battle of Halmyros</a>. The Catalans took over, and the county later passed to the Fadrique family, a branch of the royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1394 the widow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-fadrique">Louis Fadrique</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helena-kantakouzene">Helena Kantakouzene</a>, lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amfissa">Salona</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Sultan Bayezid I</a>. It was briefly held by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/despotate-of-the-morea">Despotate of the Morea</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> in the early 15th century before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took it permanently in 1410.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-salona.jpg" alt="County of Salona" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greece_in_1278.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1205 CE – 1410 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salona</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Thomas d'Autremencourt, Louis Fadrique</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French, Catalan, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lordship of Salona, Amfissa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1308&amp;focus=county-of-salona" aria-label="County of Salona on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5236 795 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Salona lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5556 1051L5563 982M5556 1051L5580 1057M5556 1051L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5563 982h0M5580 1057h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5556 1051h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5556 1051h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1308&amp;focus=county-of-salona">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

